  "raw_text": "No. Temporal proximity shows correlation, not causation.\n\nAn update occurring shortly before a failure may raise suspicion, but proving causation requires additional evidence, such as:\n\n- Reproducing the failure after applying the update\n- Showing the issue disappears after rollback\n- Identifying a plausible technical mechanism\n- Finding relevant errors in logs or diagnostics\n- Ruling out hardware defects, environmental factors, configuration changes, and other concurrent events\n- Observing the same pattern across multiple machines\n\nTiming can justify investigation, but by itself it does not prove the update caused the failure.",
